From 33ab2593621afd66257b8ec469f2a2ac2f4ff083 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duy Truong <duytruong@google.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 17:13:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix L2CAP heap overflow by enforcing minimum MPS

An attacker could trigger an integer underflow and subsequent ~65KB heap overflow by sending a crafted L2CAP CONFIG_REQ with an ERTM MPS value of 1. During L2CAP packet transmission, the Maximum PDU Payload Size (`max_pdu`) is derived from this MPS. If `max_pdu` is 1, subtracting `L2CAP_SDU_LEN_OVERHEAD` (which is 2) causes the unsigned 16-bit integer to underflow to 65535, which is then used in a buffer allocation.

This commit fixes the issue by enforcing a minimum bound for the MPS in `l2c_fcr_process_peer_cfg_req`. If the requested MPS is greater than 0 but less than 8, it is overridden to 8 and the configuration request is rejected by setting `fcr_ok = L2CAP_PEER_CFG_UNACCEPTABLE`. This prevents the `max_pdu` variable from underflowing, thereby eliminating the root cause of the heap overflow.

Test: /google/bin/releases/alint/alint && atest net_test_stack_l2cap

Bug: 511263142
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
This was autogenerated by MendIt (go/androidmendit)

Change-Id: If3482a9e8635c78492da32695cf33a1412d255b8
(cherry picked from commit c2a47d8f70ef96e417ac0aec02a80c5ec5710e3a)
---
 system/stack/l2cap/l2c_fcr.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/system/stack/l2cap/l2c_fcr.cc b/system/stack/l2cap/l2c_fcr.cc
index 60ddaff473..3924270ffc 100644
--- a/system/stack/l2cap/l2c_fcr.cc
+++ b/system/stack/l2cap/l2c_fcr.cc
@@ -1849,6 +1849,13 @@ uint8_t l2c_fcr_process_peer_cfg_req(tL2C_CCB* p_ccb, tL2CAP_CFG_INFO* p_cfg) {
                            L2CAP_SDU_LEN_OFFSET - fcs_len;
       }
 
+      /* Ensure the MPS is at least the minimum */
+      if (p_cfg->fcr.mps > 0 && p_cfg->fcr.mps < 8) {
+        p_cfg->fcr.mps = 8;
+        p_ccb->out_cfg_fcr_present = true;
+        fcr_ok = L2CAP_PEER_CFG_UNACCEPTABLE;
+      }
+
       /* Ensure the MPS is not bigger than the MTU */
       if ((p_cfg->fcr.mps == 0) || (p_cfg->fcr.mps > p_ccb->peer_cfg.mtu)) {
         p_cfg->fcr.mps = p_ccb->peer_cfg.mtu;
